## XLivelessAddon (original)

The launcher/SecuROM bypass, the save/settings path redirects, the WM_ROM message window, the
borderless window handling and the INI layout descend from
[XLivelessAddon](https://github.com/GTAmodding/XLivelessAddon) by the GTAmodding community,
released into the public domain. `source/skip_launcher.ixx`, `source/rom_window.ixx`,
`source/savegames.ixx` and `source/windowed.ixx` carry a header that attributes the bodies.

## ZolikaPatch

The recovered signature tables, the SkipLauncher stage split (main, DFA, ROM), the GFWL gating
patches and the legacy DFA file-API hooks are a reimplementation of the machine-level behaviour of
ZolikaPatch 7.65 by Zolika1351. ZolikaPatch shipped as a compiled ASI without source; no original
source is redistributed here.

## GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix

The borderless-window/focus-loss logic (`source/windowed.ixx`), the 300 ms intro-skip variant
(`SkipIntro` in `source/patches.ixx`) and the shared `Event`, `IATHook`, `find_pattern` and
byte/pattern helpers in `source/common.ixx` follow GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix (`windowed.ixx`,
`skipintro.ixx`, `common.ixx`), Copyright (C) ThirteenAG and contributors, GPL-3.0. The
per-feature FusionFix gating in `source/config.ixx` follows the same project's compatibility
approach.

## Vendored libraries (git submodules)

The `external/` directory pins the same libraries OpenPreCEPatch and FusionFix use. Their licence
texts live in their own submodule trees.

| Path | Project | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `external/injector` | [ThirteenAG/injector](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/injector) (LINK/2012, ThirteenAG) | zlib |
| `external/injector/safetyhook` | [cursey/safetyhook](https://github.com/cursey/safetyhook) | Boost 1.0 |
| `external/injector/bddisasm` | [bitdefender/bddisasm](https://github.com/bitdefender/bddisasm) | Apache-2.0 |
| `external/injector/kananlib` | [cursey/kananlib](https://github.com/cursey/kananlib) | Boost 1.0 |
| `external/injector/minhook` | [TsudaKageyu/minhook](https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook) | BSD-2-Clause |
| `external/hooking` | [ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns) (CitizenFX, NTAuthority) | MIT |
| `external/IniReader` | [ThirteenAG/IniReader](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/IniReader) | MIT |
| `external/IniReader/mINI` | [metayeti/mINI](https://github.com/metayeti/mINI) (Danijel Durakovic) | MIT |

The nested injector submodules are initialised recursively (`git submodule update --init
--recursive`) so a checkout is complete and buildable offline afterwards. Only injector's
header-only patching helpers, Hooking.Patterns and IniReader are compiled; the rest are carried
by the pinned injector revision.

The pinned `external/injector` revision is `eb42c6d` from the maintained fork at
https://github.com/SandeMC/injector. Upstream `MakeRET` stored the opcode through a deduced `int`
and therefore wrote four bytes for both `ret` and `ret imm16`; the fork stores the opcode as one
byte and the immediate as two (three bytes total for `ret imm16`). The fork is based on upstream
`1f7c3f9`, the change is a single two-line commit prepared for upstream, and the zlib licence is
unchanged.

The pinned `external/IniReader` revision (`206c4b3`) is upstream and unmodified. Upstream's
header is all-inline, and mINI crashed when it was instantiated from a C++23 module interface
unit (reproduced in this add-on's `xla.config`); `source/ini_file.cpp`, a plain TU, now owns the
reader and the module includes only the declarations in `source/ini_file.h`. The MIT licence is
unchanged.

